                <pb facs="0516" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg410"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Barrett to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-02-11"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 11,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Minister Barrett reports that three mounted men attempted to assassinate the
                    President of Colombia while he was riding in his carriage in the suburbs
                    yesterday morning by firing eight shots, five striking the carriage. He says the
                    President was uninjured and the assailants escaped. The city is quiet, although
                    there was much excitement and indignation at the cowardly attempt.</p>
            </div>
